WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.035
-Our next guest is
an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.204
you know from shows like
"The White Lotus" and "Girls,"

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:06.806
as well as
the film "Obvious Child."

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.508
He stars in
"A Friend of the Family,"

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.876
which is streaming on Peacock,

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.045
with new episodes
premiering Thursdays.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.379
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.581
-You'd just love it up there.

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.250
There's a theater
right next to the fun center.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.053
They put on plays
every weekend.

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:23.189
But -- Oh...

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.628
-Well, maybe, you know,

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:31.731
I could come and work
for you there this summer.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.967
Like how I worked
at the freight outlet.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.405
-You know, Dolly,
I hadn't thought of that.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.675
You might have just
solved all our problems.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.912
-Please welcome to the show
Jake Lacy, everybody.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.181
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:02.094
Welcome.
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:03.729
-Man, thanks for having me.
Thank you, thank you.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.665
-I've been a fan of yours
for a long time.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.802
And I feel like the first act of
your career, if you will,

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:11.137
you were known for
playing nice guys.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.471
And then we did some digging.

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:15.474
These are all just headlines
about you being nice guys

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.410
in every show you were in.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.611
-Yeah.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.747
-And then you took a turn in
"White Lotus."

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.015
You played maybe --
don't take this the wrong way --

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:24.583
the best [bleep]
in the last 10 years.

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:25.885
-Thank you, thank you.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.620
-But Now you're really --
This is a full --

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.621
You're playing
a full monster in this one.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.889
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.791
I mean, like, "White lotus,"
you hope people go like,

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.792
"Oh, am I that guy?

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.260
Like, do I treat
people that way?"

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.561
And this, if anyone sees it

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:36.963
and goes look like,
"Do I do that?",

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.965
you'd be like, "We should --
Someone should --

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.399
The authorities
should seek you out."

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:41.501
-Yeah. Right?

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.735
You should put yourself
right in jail.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.737
-There's some gray area
about that, you know?

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:48.774
-But you are -- He's a monster
who is presenting as a nice guy.

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:51.110
So I guess it is
pulling on some of your skills.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.346
-Yeah, there's --
It's like, for --

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.548
You know, not to be like,
"I'm a bad person,"

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:58.250
but, like, the,
you know, roles that, like,

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.554
I've been known for for being,
like, a good guy or a nice guy,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.389
like, that's acting, you know?

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.225
-Right.
-It's a role, you know?

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.258
-Yeah.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:07.727
-And then this is
sort of like,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.528
"What if it's not me
doing this role,

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.931
but, like, a person doing
that role to everyone

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:15.134
and their family
and community and world

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:18.738
because their motives,
at heart, are horrific?"

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.840
-This -- It is
a horrific true story.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.545
You did have the blessing of
the family that was victimized.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.480
That must make a huge difference

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.614
when you approach
something like this,

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:29.982
because it seems so sensitive.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:32.885
-Yeah, Jan Broberg, who --
You know, this is her story,

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:36.455
and she's the girl
who was taken.

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:39.258
This is -- She was a producer
and creatively involved.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:42.628
And if she hadn't been, I
wouldn't have been a part of it.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.997
Because I think would have just
lent itself to being

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:47.267
voyeuristic and sort of
grotesque in a way.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:52.405
And she has been so,
like, kind and supportive

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.940
and championing
and carries herself

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:58.778
with a level of grace that,
like, I can't even imagine.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.148
-It's a really -- It's a --
I mean, it's a haunting show,

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.516
but it is also
incredibly gripping,

00:03:04.516 --> 00:03:05.884
and you guys have done
an incredible job.

00:03:05.884 --> 00:03:08.187
And I -- You know, it's,
I guess, a little bit over

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.589
a year now where you were in,
I feel like,

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:13.526
the show of the year,
"The White Lotus."

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.827
And you mentioned the people.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:15.828
You did play
this character, Shane.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:16.962
-Yeah.

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:18.731
-And do you get approached
by people who see

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.167
a little Shane either in
themselves or loved ones?

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:24.003
-Yeah. Yes. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:27.006
Like, there's, like,
this sliding scale of people

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.941
who come up and are like,
"I saw --"

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:31.377
You know, like,
"I worry that maybe I do that."

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.979
And you go, "Oh, that's cool,"
you know?

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:35.614
And then there's people who are
like, "That's me, man!

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:39.018
[ Laughs ] I'm that guy!"

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.087
You're like, "Oh.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.521
That's great."
You know?

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:44.490
Or like, "My wife --" You know,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.858
It's, like, always with,
like, their wife there

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.059
being like, "He is like that."

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.461
They're like,
"She's always telling people!

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:51.964
That's him, you know?"

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.365
"Good, good."

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:56.535
-Top to bottom,
what a stellar cast that was.

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:59.272
And, yet, I feel you
probably get this a lot.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.607
What was it like to work with
Jennifer Coolidge?

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.409
-She's the -- I mean,
she's incredible, right?

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.945
Like -- She -- On our first --

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.081
So, we're staying at,
like, the hotel.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.216
And we couldn't leave.
It's a bubble, you know?

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.751
And we could order food in.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:15.154
So, there's like one Thai place
that really crushes it locally.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.189
And -- But they stop taking
orders at 8:00,

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:19.458
and it's like 7:56 or whatever.

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.760
And, somehow,
Jennifer's managed to get there

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.095
two days later
than the rest of us,

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:24.364
which I also don't know how --

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.665
They were like,
"You've got to be here."

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.533
And she was like,
"I'll figure it out."

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:32.438
And, so, it's just, like,
down to the wire.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.873
And we're sitting like this,
and Jennifer's here.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.442
I'm like, "Jennifer, do you want
to get in on this order?"

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.176
And she was like,
"What do they have?"

00:04:38.176 --> 00:04:41.480
Like, show her the thing,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:42.748
and she's, like, scanning.

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:44.016
She's like,
"What are you having?"

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:47.019
And I was like, "I'm just --
We're so close.

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:48.955
Like, just do it, man!"

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:51.791
And, you know, I'm,
like, kind of trying to be cool.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.392
We've known each other
for six hours.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:57.563
And also being like, "If you
don't do this, I don't eat.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.298
Like, let's go."

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:02.067
And, finally, she, like,
hands me the phone,

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:06.605
and she turns and she goes,
"You know, you're Shane."

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:09.142
And I was like...

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:12.311
And she's like -- Now when I see
her, she's like, "Mike knows.

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:13.746
Mike knows, man.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.415
Everyone thinks you're a nice
guy, but Mike sees who you are."

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:19.118
I was like, "Okay.
Thank you, Jennifer."

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.587
So, I love her, but that's,
like, the foot we got off on

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:22.955
was me like, "Let's go!"

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.490
-Yeah.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.359
I do think, though, that is --
As much fun as it would be

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:28.761
to hang out with
Jennifer Coolidge,

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.864
needing her to order Thai food
fast would maybe not be...

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:36.569
-So, then, I mean --
Look, Jennifer, I love you.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.471
This is what happened, though.

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:40.106
Then I go, "I'm gonna order
you something."

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:41.507
So we place this order.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:45.411
It arrives.
And then she disappears.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:48.281
She's gone for
the rest of the night.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.950
I see her the next day and go
like, "You never got your food."

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.118
And she's like,
"I didn't know you ordered it."

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:56.589
I was like...

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.891
This was our whole night
was this.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.225
Like...yeah.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:03.496
-Well, that really is --
I think if you're really Shane,

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:05.431
it's nice to know that
she's really Jennifer Coolidge.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.499
-That's right. That's right.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:08.735
Two authentic people
finally meeting.

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:09.836
-Hey, thanks so much
for being here.

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.903
-Dude, thank you.
-The show is outstanding.

00:06:11.903 --> 00:06:13.205
Jake Lacy, everybody.

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:14.674
"A Friend of the Family"
is streaming on Peacock,

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.175
with new episodes
premiering Thursdays.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.878
We'll be right back
with music from Pusha T.

